course: dictionary
lesson: 2680
title: Tiny living things in the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A diatom is a very small living thing, far too small to see without a microscope. You can work out its meaning from the words around it: «Diatoms are single-celled algae with glass shells in beautiful patterns.» Single-celled means made of just one cell, and algae are simple living things that often live in water.
explain: Read the next clue: «they make a big share of the oxygen we breathe.» A big share means a large part, so diatoms help make the air we breathe. Check your meaning by swapping it in: diatoms are tiny, but they are important for the whole world's air.
explain: Scientists often mention «plankton and diatoms» together, so diatoms are one of the small living things that float in water. Their shells are made of a glassy material called silica, which is why they can look like little patterned jewels under a microscope.
fact: A diatom is a tiny living thing made of just one cell.
fact: Diatoms are a kind of algae that live in water.
fact: Diatoms have glassy shells made of silica, and the shells often have beautiful patterns.
fact: Diatoms make a large part of the oxygen we breathe.
fact: Diatoms are food for many sea animals.
fact: Empty diatom shells can pile up on the sea floor over a long time.
exercise: «Diatoms are single-celled algae with glass shells in beautiful patterns.» What does single-celled mean? | *Made of just one cell | Able to swim fast | Made of hundreds of tiny shells | Made of glass
exercise: Priya says diatoms are animals with legs. What is the correct idea? | Diatoms are big fish that swim in rivers | *Diatoms are tiny living things, like algae, not animals with legs | Diatoms are rocks on the sea floor | Diatoms are a type of sand
exercise: «They make a big share of the oxygen we breathe.» What does a big share mean? | A dish of food for animals | *A large part | A small piece to keep | A bright light in the water
test: Copy the word from «Diatoms are single-celled algae with glass shells in beautiful patterns.» that names the material their shells are made of. | single | *glass | algae | patterns
test: Why would you need a microscope to look at a diatom? | Because it is made of gold | Because it can talk to you | Because it is bigger than a whale | *Because it is far too small to see with your eyes
exam: Which sentence best describes a diatom? | A giant whale that lives on land | *A tiny living thing in water with a glassy shell | A large rock on a mountain | A kind of cloud that floats above the sea
